// @@@ If the index is greater than or equal to 0 and less than the current size of the vector, then for every integer i such that i is greater than the index and less than the size of the vector before it was modified minus one, the element at position i in the vector after the operation is either null if the element at position i+1 before the operation was null, or equal to the element at position i+1 before the operation.
